  Quote of the Week:

  "It is a political error to practice deceit, if deceit is carried too 
far."
  -Frederick II, King of Prussia, 1740.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Stormy winter gave way to spring, and Prometeo prepared to carry out his 
imperial orders.  He attempted a Tornado spell, but botched it.  A strange 
magical counterspell seemed to have impeded his spell.

  In Shasta, Prometeo brought to bay the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
Prometeo commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were commanded by the 
provincial Eagle chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Shasta (0304):

