  DEFENDING ARMY

  Prometeo stood determinedly at the head of his thousands.  No generals 
were present to lead the forces of the provincial Eagle chieftain.
  As luck would have it, Prometeo's formations were partially concealed by 
some rocks, giving them a slight edge.  Further, Prometeo maneuvered his 
forces against the provincial Eagle chieftain with great tactical judgement 
and consequently obtained an important tactical superiority.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 231st Legion were stiffened by a 
tough band of freedom fighters of the Mercenaries Guild, who led them into a 
fanatical fervor by example of their fearless elan.  They were arrayed 
against the Veteran 30th Eagles.  The 30th Eagles swooped down on the 231st 
Legion and attacked without mercy.  In this match, a stray gryphon 
unexpectedly appeared, disordering the 30th Eagles and creating some 
apprehension.  It appeared probable that the 231st Legion would win the 
battle.
  But would defeat now be snatched from the jaws of victory?  The 231st 
Legion carelessly blundered into a nest of booby traps and lost some of 
their best front-line troops.  Still, the 231st Legion fought with the 30th 
Eagles and gradually pushed them back.
  The battle ended in victory for the soldiers of Prometeo as they broke 
through the lines at a critical moment.
  Although Prometeo's host were victorious, the provincial Eagle chieftain 
rallied its men and decided to contest Shasta.
  With the coming of the early summer season Prometeo marched on Katanga 
(#404) with his forces.  Viewing the eastern horizon, one can see a Plain 
province known as Chaco (#504).  It is said that 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns there.  It is known to be 
populated by Elves.  Their Elven fighters fight as Phalanx and Heavy Cavalry.
To the southeast there is a Desert province known as Trouthome (#505), a 
prosperous land of Elves where Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns.  
Their Elven fighters prefer to array themselves in the style of Phalanx.  
Prometeo discovered a feature in Katanga: a Cave (#61) occupied by 
the Succubus.  Legend says the Necronomicon is hidden here.  The Succubus is 
a strong, evil and seductive demon capable of luring an adventurer to his 
death with her seductive charms.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  Prometeo 
cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to Prometeo.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  Prometeo attempted an illegal move.  
He was ordered to move from Katanga to Cantia, further than his army could 
move.  Instead, he practiced his Druidism diligently for months, but could 
make no progress.

  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Jungle province of Katanga, 
ruled by Circe (#8).  Pascal (#78) commanded the attacking armies.  The 
defenders were led by Prometeo.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Katanga (0404):

