  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with her warriors was Tlazolteotl.  Prometeo stood 
ready at the head of his thousands.
  Tlazolteotl strode forward and challenged Prometeo to honorable combat.  
Prometeo accepted the challenge to honorable combat.  Raising her hands high 
in the air, Tlazolteotl cast a Gate Demon spell and an extra-dimensional 
gate appeared, and out of it sprang a terrifying demon!  Prometeo waved his 
hands, meaning to cast a Psychic Blast spell, but it backfired and a dove 
tumbled out of his hat instead.  Uttering her words of magic with breathless 
precision, the Succubus let fly a Psychic Blast spell, projecting psychic 
waves of stunning force towards Prometeo.  His spell was disrupted by the 
event.  Prometeo could do nothing but stand and stare in his stunned state.

  The Succubus cautiously advanced to bow range.  In his pathetic stunned 
state, Prometeo could not determine what to do about his predicament.
  The Succubus closed to melee range, seething with uncontrolled blood-lust. 
Prometeo stood stunned, unable to regain his balance.  The Succubus 
acrobatically flipped over Prometeo and swang at him and scorched him with 1 
damage points.  Now the effects of the stun finally wore off and Prometeo 
prepared to renew his attack.
  The Succubus then swang at Prometeo with maximum force but her aim was 
slightly off.  Prometeo viciously thrust at the Succubus and damaged 
the Succubus, scoring 8 damage points.  The Succubus thrust at Prometeo with 
all her might and walloped him with 1 damage points.  Prometeo swang at his 
vaunted nemesis and inflicted 5 damage points.  Seeking to exploit a gap in 
his defenses, the Succubus skillfully thrust at him and scored 2 damage 
points on him.
  Prometeo whirled about and swang at the Succubus and scored on 
the Succubus, doing 5 points of damage.  The Succubus swang at Prometeo and 
missed badly.  Showing no fear, Prometeo swang at the Succubus and damaged 
the Succubus, inflicting 9 damage points.  The Succubus fell, fatally 
injured.  The illusion dissipated and was dispelled.  Gesturing with her 
hands, Tlazolteotl juxtaposed otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Hand 
Of Death spell and began making squeezing motions with her hands.
  Tlazolteotl wrapped her phantasmal hand around Prometeo's heart and 
squeezed it viciously and walloped Prometeo with 3 damage points.
  Prometeo quickly moved to bow range.  Tlazolteotl brought her hands 
together and yanked them apart in a tearing motion, provoking a 
blood-curdling squeal from Prometeo and inflicted 3 damage points.
  Prometeo rushed into melee combat.  He angrily attacked Tlazolteotl and 
would have struck her if Tlazolteotl hadn't sidestepped just then.  The 
invisible hands of Tlazolteotl grasped his lungs, choking the life out of 
Prometeo and scored 3 damage points on Prometeo.  Prometeo was mortally 
wounded.  And so it came to pass that Prometeo met his tragic end.
  The forces commanded by Prometeo were disheartened by his demise, yet 
still they pressed ahead with some hope of victory.  As luck would have it, 
Tlazolteotl's formations were partially concealed by a sudden mist, giving 
them a small edge.  Also, Tlazolteotl maneuvered her forces against the 
acting commander with excellent tactical judgement and enjoyed an important 
tactical advantage.
  Calling upon his arcane Spell of Oratory, Prometeo started with an 
inspiring speech to his army, raising their courage.
  On the right flank, the Crack 222nd Phalanx were arrayed against the 
Veteran 262nd Heavy Cavalry.  The 75th Dragons swooped down on the 262nd 
Heavy Cavalry and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 75th Dragons to the fore, angling for a better 
match-up.  The poor horses of the 262nd Heavy Cavalry were spooked by the 
Beasts they beheld.  The 75th Dragons battled with the 262nd Heavy Cavalry 
and squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  Within the interior lines, the Crack 223rd Phalanx were arrayed against 
the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The 256th Dragons swooped down on the 24th 
Heavy Cavalry and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 256th Dragons to the front line, as a strategem 
for a superior match-up.  The nervous horses of the 24th Heavy Cavalry were 
frightened by the Beasts they were faced with.  The 256th Dragons fought 
with the 24th Heavy Cavalry and mowed them down like weeds.
  On the left outside wing, the Crack 139th Phalanx faced the Veteran 231st 
Legion.  The clumsy mass of the 139th Phalanx was tested by the maneuverable 
Legionnaires.  The 106th Dragons soared over the 231st Legion and attacked 
without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 106th Dragons to the fore, as a strategem for a 
superior nemesis effect.  On this field, the 106th Dragons immediately 
turned in flight when they contacted their enemy.  But it soon became clear 
that the retreat was a feigned one, a trick to lure their enemy into 
overextending himself.  The 106th Dragons fought with the 231st Legion and 
advanced at will.
  The forces of Tlazolteotl broke through the lines of their opposition and 
were victorious.  The 75th Dragons destroyed the 262nd Heavy Cavalry.  The 
256th Dragons annihilated the 24th Heavy Cavalry.  The 106th Dragons 
demolished the 231st Legion.
  Tlazolteotl's host concluded the campaign victoriously and conquered the 
province of Katanga.  Its forces completely dispersed, the acting commander 
escaped frightened and alone to Cantia.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Prometeo treated with his ally Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo 
treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Adhemar (#28) arose one morning with a whim to see Chandrapur, and so left 
from Tesawa to travel to that province.
  Drago (#39) hiked into Cantia.  He had grown tired with Big Sky and was 
drawn there by rumors of its fine wines and even finer champagnes.
  Ashley (#74) heard that an old buddy was pearl-diving in Tesawa and left 
Mare Imbrium to see his old friend.

  Cantia was raided by the Werewolf, who stormed from out of the dark and 
pillaged or destroyed 2 gold worth of property.
  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 51 gold in revenue.  10 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 158th Dragons trained well and improved in quality.  20 gold 
was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left with 54 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Mortimer, Squire to Tarsus
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Tarsus set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He rode his flying armies over to Orielle.  Tarsus found 
some time to investigate Orielle while marching.  100% of it has been 
explored to date.  His efforts raised his prowess in Marches.
  In early summer, Tarsus flew over to Shasta.
  Marlon could not cast Oratory on Tarsus because Tarsus was in another 
province.  So, Marlon discovered nothing valuable in his sagely researches.

  Prometeo ordered an invasion force into the Mountain province of Shasta, 
owned by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  Tarsus was in command of the 
invading armies.  The defenders were led by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

