  The attackers had the 158th Dragons in reserve.  Standing at the ready 
with his warriors was Tarsus.  No generals were present to lead the forces 
of the provincial Eagle chieftain.
  The fortunes of war turned against Tarsus when his best scout troops fell 
into a clever ambush and were annihilated.  The provincial Eagle chieftain's 
horde thus gained a tremendous advantage.  As the fierce battle intensified, 
the tactical abilities of the provincial Eagle chieftain and Tarsus seemed 
evenly matched and neither general could achieve a tactical advantage.
  Tarsus was frustrated by the Dragons, who could not comprehend his 
commands.
  Across the whole front, the Elite 25th Legion faced the Veteran 30th 
Eagles.  The 46th Dragons swooped down on the 30th Eagles and attacked 
without mercy.  The 30th Eagles swooped down on the 25th Legion and attacked 
them.  Here, the 30th Eagles were rallied by the speech of an officer who 
shouted "Do you think you can live forever?  Charge!  !  !"  Even with the 
30th Eagles's good luck, the 25th Legion fought the 30th Eagles and moved 
ahead slowly, contested for every yard of their advance.
  Tarsus's great horde overpowered the army of the provincial Eagle 
chieftain and took the field, dispersing their enemies.
  Tarsus's campaign accomplished the conquest of Shasta.  The 30th Eagles 
were unable to retreat and disbanded into mercenaries.
  In fall, Tarsus flew into Moongard.  To the southeast there lies a Sea 
province known as the Io Sea (#406), an area of no races where 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango reigns.  Viewing the southwestern horizon, 
one can see a Mountain province called Big Sky (#306).  It is said that 
Bradipo I is the ruler there.  It is known to be occupied by Dwarves.  Their 
Dwarven warriors array themselves in the style of Axemen.

