  Tlazolteotl maneuvered the 256th Dragons to the front line, as a strategem 
for a better nemesis effect.  The 25th Legion fought the 256th Dragons and 
was forced to retreat in disorder.
  Out on the right flank, the Crack 23rd Legion faced the Crack 222nd 
Phalanx.  The 158th Dragons soared over the 106th Dragons and attacked them. 
The clumsy mass of the 222nd Phalanx was shaken by the flexible 
Legionnaires.  The unwieldy mass of the 223rd Phalanx was severely tested by 
the maneuverable Legionnaires.  The 106th Dragons swooped down on the 158th 
Dragons and attacked without mercy.
  Tlazolteotl switched the 106th Dragons to the front line, angling for a 
better match-up.  The 23rd Legion battled with the 106th Dragons and was 
powerless to halt their advance.
  The forces of Tlazolteotl broke through the lines of their opposition and 
were victorious.  The 256th Dragons annihilated the 25th Legion.  The 106th 
Dragons destroyed the 23rd Legion.  The 75th Dragons scattered the 46th 
Dragons in all directions.  The 106th Dragons overtook the enemy and slew 
the 45th Legion almost to a man.  The 75th Dragons gave chase and demolished 
the 49th Legion.
  The attacking Kingdom was defeated and turned back in its attempt to take 
Moongard.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  the long campaign 
caused the 158th Dragons to lose some of its battle-lust, and now it can 
only be counted on to fight as a Green unit.  Her forces completely 
destroyed, Adele (#83) escaped frightened and alone to Mongu.  The acting 
commander pulled back to Shasta with its command.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Tarsus


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I moved into Macondo.  During my travels this season, a 
Renegade Swordsman unexpectedly rushed at me from out of nowhere.  I raised 
my arms, meaning to cast a Telekinetic Storm spell, but it backfired and a 
dove tumbled out of my hat instead.  My efforts raised my prowess in Psychic 
Magic.
  The Renegade Swordsman moved into bow range.  Gesturing with my arms, I 
juxtaposed otherworldly forces of magic, casting a Charm spell.  I 
befriended the Renegade Swordsman and used my respite to get away.

  With the advent of the early summer season I could not cast Oratory on 
Tarsus because Tarsus was in another province.  So, I discovered nothing 
valuable in my sagely researches.
  I heard a rumor telling of a feature in Macondo (#205) previously unknown 
to us, a Sacred Rock where dwells the Renegade Archer.  The Sacred Rock is 
reputed to contain the Large Hoard of Gold.
  In late summer, I moved into Orielle.  While adventuring, I saw no 
monsters.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  I invented nothing in my sagely 
researches.
  While talking to some friendly farmers, I heard a rumor about a Cave in 
Mongu (#305), occupied by the Renegade Swordsman.  Some maintain that 
the Renegade Swordsman owns the Large Hoard of Gold.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I discovered nothing in my 
sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, in his sagely researches, Ishtar discovered a fabulous 
invention called the Ice Cream Cone!  The following benefits are conferred 
by the Ice Cream Cone:
  The Ice Cream Cone is a nice little Royal Monopoly which will also boost 
revenue from your Toothpaste Monopoly.  You can increase your Kingdom's 
revenue by an average of 1% each gameturn.

  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Ishtar tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his natural ability.  He invented 
nothing worthy of note in his sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer came.  Ishtar tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his natural aptitude.  He 
discovered nothing in his sagely researches.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  In his sagely researches, 
Ishtar discovered a fabulous invention called the Vulcanized Rubber!  The 
following benefits are conferred by the Vulcanized Rubber:
  Rubber has a thousand uses.  Your 25-year-old heir is especially thankful 
for the rubber ducky made for him by the Royal Toymaker.    The effect of 
this invention is to raise the revenue of the Kingdom by an average of 4% 
each gameturn.

  With the advent of the early winter season, Ishtar invented nothing in his 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Girard's attempted cast of the Plague spell didn't work.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I rode into 
Marzuq.
  With the advent of the late summer season, I travelled to Plumwood.
  In fall, I journeyed to Birchwood.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  I recruited enough men in 
Birchwood to create the 152nd Legion, the 160th Legion, the 168th 
Heavy Cavalry and the 199th Heavy Cavalry for the army of Girard.

  Thy humble servant,   Girard


